properties.takeoff_description:
'Heimat': mostly used in the morning;
'Galvera': used in the afternoon;
HG-Ramp in front of cable car station

2 TOs available:
- Kamel: less than 10' walk from train station;
- Chrüterwand: very steep, nowadays seldom used.

Different TO's available!
- HG's takeoff right underneath gondola;
- South TO: take off : 47.2837N, 9.4133E;
- North TO: as indicated on map: 3min walk from gondola.

- TO 'South' (2300): from gondola follow track to left, in winter along skislope; about 7min; windsock; easy;
- TO 'North' (2280m): 3min from gondola, follow track to the right; with moderate N-winds soaring and toplanding possible.
ATTENTION: cable

- TO 'Jakobshorn Gipfel': 3min from cable car peak station; windsock on top of mountain; 
- TO 'Jatzhütte': 10min from cable car (see picture): S-SW-W; easy.
- TO 'Brämabüel': in winter by chair lift; in summer to be reached only by walking about 20min from  the Jakobshorn peak

- TO 'North': 5min from Gondola station; windsock; summer and winter; easy; with moderate N-winds dynamic soaring possible; 
Route of flight: via 'Gotschnagrat' to LZ 'Klosters'
- TO 'South': between gondola station and restaurant; summer and winter; DIFFICULT! - only for experienved pilots; Route of flight: LZ 'Davos -Bolgen'

steep, grassy meadow;
also suitable for beginners
>> do NOT park your car in the village!
